    "machine": "-",
    "text": "Done — the design passed the full reference grade. 🎉\n\n## Two triangles → **ELIGIBLE** on BB [[144,12,12]]\n\n**The design**\n- **Large triangle** = one closed loop of **144 sites** (side ~50, corners cut to 120° so it clears the min-angle rule while still reading as a triangle). This loop carries the data qubits — it's the conveyor belt the BB circuit rides.\n- **Smaller triangle** = **24 docks**, spread evenly one unit inside the three sides. Each is a gate-capable trap on its own rail off the loop; together they trace the inner triangle.\n- Why not two independent triangles: the conveyor drives only one loop, so a second free-standing loop could never exchange qubits with the first. Making the inner shape the docks is what actually lets the checks run.\n\n**The grade** (reference evaluator, Lean certificate included — every stage passed):\n- **T_jones = 496.84 ms** per syndrome round (the ranked metric — beats the 522 ms reference ring)\n- Transport 397.25 ms · 46 DACs · 5066 instructions\n- Where time goes: transport ~60% (undock 134 ms, dock 85 ms, shuttle 78 ms), cooling ~31%, gates ~5%, the rest measurement/reset\n- Junction load is even across all 24 junctions, so nothing is bottlenecked on a single point\n\nThis result is **local and not published** — it shows in your Studio Results as \"Local result – not published.\" Publishing to the shared leaderboard needs your approval; just say the word and I'll show you exactly what would be uploaded (`qccd_prepare_publish`) before anything leaves your machine."
